# Data for the full J₄ normal-subgroup calculation

The 788 rows are explicit lists of masks in the existing 21 candidate words.
No normality, order, rank, or completeness statement is assumed. The two row
maps merely divide the required checks into 595 small-Frattini obligations
and 193 comparisons with the existing candidates. All indices are zero-based;
comments retain the one-based GAP row. Square and inverse-conjugacy tables
also remain unproved input data. See `source/generate.py` for provenance.

Source context: Aschbacher–Smith, printed p.511/PDF p.528, citing Asc86b.
-/

